[[File:SentinelMapEncounter.png|thumb|right|A broken Sentinel found in a map]]
'''Sentinels''' are a [[league mechanic]] introduced in the [[Sentinel league]]. Sentinels can be activated to have them fire beams that empower a limited number of monsters and improve their item drops.

Sentinels have a chance to randomly appear in [[map]]s and can be guaranteed to appear via an explicit modifier.

==Mechanics==
Maps containing a Sentinel encounter will have a buried Sentinel with random modifiers spawn near the starting portal. Players can interact with it to repair it, granting the ability to deploy it in that area by clicking on the button or using the corresponding hotkey.

When a Sentinel is deployed, it will follow the player around for a duration, firing beams at nearby monsters to empower them. Monsters recover to full life when gaining Empowerment. Empowerment increases damage dealt and reduces damage taken by the monster, but also increases the experience, item rarity, and item quantity of the monster when killed. Empowering an enemy also has a chance for it to gain an additional reward, displayed by an icon over them. 

The Sentinel will disappear once it has empowered a set number of enemies, is dismissed manually, when the Sentinel's duration expires, or if the player dies or leaves the instance.

===Types of Sentinels===
There are three types of Sentinels:

Red '''Stalker''' Sentinels fire beams periodically to empower enemies.

Blue '''Pandemonium''' Sentinels fire a beam only once, chaining to multiple enemies. Unlike the other types, they deplete after firing their beam once, even if it didn't get to empower the maximum number of enemies.

Yellow '''Apex''' Sentinels fire a beam to empower enemies, but only target Rare and Unique monsters.

